{"type":"assistant","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I fixed the override bug in `merge_config`. It used to apply an override only when the value was truthy, so `0`, `\"\"`, `False`, `None` or an empty list were silently dropped. For example, `{\"retries\": 3}` merged with `{\"retries\": 0}` kept `3`. Now any key present in the override replaces the base value, whatever it is.\n\nThe function body is now just `dict(base)` followed by `out.update(override)`, which still returns a new dict and leaves `base` unchanged. I also replaced the old \"BUG:\" comment with a short docstring.\n\nThe two existing tests pass. I also ran a quick check that overrides of `0`, `\"\"`, `False`, `[]` and `None` all win and that `base` isn't modified.\n\nI left `old_merge_config` alone. Nothing in this repo calls it, but its TODO says the v1 loader still uses it, and that loader may live outside this repo. It now benefits from the same fix. The TODOs in `rows.py` and `format.py` are unrelated to config loading, so I didn't touch them."}]},"session_id":"2a1dfdc3-ed63-4339-b685-114616332784"}
{"type":"result","subtype":"success","duration_ms":33438,"duration_api_ms":33438,"is_error":false,"result":"I'll start by reading the config loader and anything around it.I fixed the override bug in `merge_config`. It used to apply an override only when the value was truthy, so `0`, `\"\"`, `False`, `None` or an empty list were silently dropped. For example, `{\"retries\": 3}` merged with `{\"retries\": 0}` kept `3`. Now any key present in the override replaces the base value, whatever it is.\n\nThe function body is now just `dict(base)` followed by `out.update(override)`, which still returns a new dict and leaves `base` unchanged. I also replaced the old \"BUG:\" comment with a short docstring.\n\nThe two existing tests pass. I also ran a quick check that overrides of `0`, `\"\"`, `False`, `[]` and `None` all win and that `base` isn't modified.\n\nI left `old_merge_config` alone. Nothing in this repo calls it, but its TODO says the v1 loader still uses it, and that loader may live outside this repo. It now benefits from the same fix. The TODOs in `rows.py` and `format.py` are unrelated to config loading, so I didn't touch them.","session_id":"2a1dfdc3-ed63-4339-b685-114616332784","request_id":"0245da68-7d27-4025-ab06-104872ab42b4","usage":{"inputTokens":14,"outputTokens":1781,"cacheReadTokens":138042,"cacheWriteTokens":18252}}
